WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:02.490
The Evil Dead can never die.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.990
From the new cast to what that 'R' rating
means, here's everything you need to know

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.717
about Evil Dead Rise.

00:00:07.717 --> 00:00:08.991
Let's go.

00:00:09.424 --> 00:00:14.090
Originally, Evil Dead Rise was headed for
HBO Max, but a funny thing happened on the

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.160
way to the streamer.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:21.500
First, David Zaslav decided to emphasize theatrical
releases after taking over Warner Bros. Secondly,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.439
Deadline reports that when the film's trailer
played at the trade show CineEurope, people

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:28.880
ate it up, proving the film was good enough
for theaters.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.750
So when can we expect to get in line and buy
some tickets?

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:37.680
Well, we'll get to see Evil Dead Rise hit
theaters on April 21, 2023, as announced via

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.630
Bruce Campbell's Twitter account.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:44.500
The actor also shared a first-look photo of
the film, which showed a smiling Deadite leering

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.300
through an apartment's blood-soaked peephole.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.210
Interestingly enough, when Evil Dead Rise
releases in 2023, it won't be the only horror-comedy

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:52.710
that month.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:57.270
The flick will be competing against Renfield,
which stars Nicholas Hoult as Renfield and

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.699
Nicolas Cage as his master, Dracula.

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:03.036
It'll be interesting to see which horror-comedy
walks away dominant.

00:01:03.036 --> 00:01:04.976
"Now, let's eat!"

00:01:06.335 --> 00:01:09.880
Throughout the Evil Dead franchise, there
has been one constant — someone reads an

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.430
evil book and unleashes the forces of hell.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.290
In the first two Evil Dead movies, we watch
this horror show play out in a cabin in the

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:20.948
middle of nowhere, with a group of young people
getting picked off and possessed by sadistic demons.

00:01:20.948 --> 00:01:24.540
Of course, the big difference between the
two films is that The Evil Dead is more or

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.511
less straight horror while Evil Dead II is
much heavier on the comedy.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.755
"Who's laughing now?"

00:01:33.755 --> 00:01:38.100
Things get weird in Army of Darkness when
franchise hero Ash Williams goes back to the

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.570
Middle Ages to fight a skeleton army.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.060
And in 2013's Evil Dead, things get gorier
than ever when a group of friends hole up

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.390
in a cabin and release the Deadites.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.330
But what will Evil Dead Rise be about?

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:53.811
Will it follow the standard Evil Dead formula
of a cabin in the woods, or will it get a

00:01:53.811 --> 00:01:56.159
bit more creative a la Army of Darkness?

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:00.630
Well, this time, the Deadites are headed to
Los Angeles, and they plan to unleash havoc

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.220
on an apartment complex.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.729
The official synopsis reads,

00:02:03.729 --> 00:02:08.179
"[A] road-weary Beth pays an overdue visit
to her older sister Ellie [...] The sisters'

00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:12.580
reunion is cut short by the discovery of a
mysterious book deep in the bowels of Ellie's

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:17.099
building, giving rise to flesh-possessing
demons and thrusting Beth into a primal battle

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:18.747
for survival."

00:02:18.747 --> 00:02:23.590
In the first three Evil Dead films the franchise
was anchored by the shotgun-toting, chainsaw-wielding

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.580
Ash Williams, played by the one and only Bruce
Campbell.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.281
"Shop smart.

00:02:28.594 --> 00:02:30.454
Shop S-Mart…you got that??"

00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:37.190
In the 2013 installment, the focus shifted
to Mia, played by Jane Levy, a woman struggling

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:41.769
with drug addiction who must also face an
onslaught from hell when she tries to go cold

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:42.769
turkey.

00:02:42.769 --> 00:02:44.909
So who will be leading Evil Dead Rise?

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:48.700
Lily Sullivan will be playing the lead role
of Beth, who goes to visit her single mom

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.970
sister and finds herself facing an apartment
complex full of Deadites.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:57.970
You may have seen Sullivan in miniseries like
Picnic at Hanging Rock or movies like Mental.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.041
Opposite her, Alyssa Sutherland will play
Ellie, the mother of three living in the apartment

00:03:02.041 --> 00:03:07.801
complex, whose life gets even more complicated
with the appearance of the flesh-bound Necronomicon.

00:03:07.965 --> 00:03:13.129
The first three Evil Dead films were famously
directed by Sam Raimi, who went from microbudget

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:16.800
filmmaker to mainstream director on the success
of this trilogy.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.910
The 2013 Evil Dead was helmed by Fede Álvarez,
who kept things intense with his two other

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:25.230
features — Don't Breathe and The Girl in
the Spider's Web.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:29.230
So who's in charge of all the mayhem, murder,
and madness this time around?

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.459
Evil Dead Rise will be directed by Lee Cronin.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:35.350
Sure, he isn't a household name yet, but we
have a feeling he will be soon.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:40.269
At the moment, Cronin has just one released
film to his name — 2019's uber-creepy The

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:41.620
Hole in the Ground.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:45.510
That film follows a single mother in Ireland
who suspects her son might not actually be

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.510
her boy anymore.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:51.230
Raimi, who's also the executive producer on
Evil Dead Rise, was so impressed with Cronin's

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.549
work that he hand-picked him to direct the
new Evil Dead film.

00:03:54.549 --> 00:03:56.650
Speaking with /Film, Raimi said,

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.099
"'I loved 'The Hole in the Ground.'

00:03:58.099 --> 00:04:00.370
[...] I thought, 'This is a really great director.'

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:04.099
And we met, and we talked, and he said he
really liked 'The Evil Dead.'

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:06.590
And I said, 'Then why don't you make the new
one?

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:09.360
I think you're just the kind [of] guy I'd
like to do it."

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:13.611
That's high praise from the man who conjured
the Evil Dead franchise into existence.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.950
The two people most closely associated with
the Evil Dead franchise are the two who brought

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:22.010
the series to life — director Sam Raimi
and star Bruce Campbell.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:25.650
Without these titans of horror, we wouldn't
have Ash Williams duking it out with undead

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:29.990
monsters, sawing off his own possessed hand,
or reigning supreme as the king of S-Mart.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.890
However, neither one will be reprising their
original positions for Evil Dead Rise.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.460
So will these two be involved with Evil Dead
Rise?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.210
Fortunately, the answer is yes.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:44.020
Both Raimi and Campbell will be serving as
executive producers, along with Robert Tapert,

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:46.650
who's been involved with the franchise since
the first film.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:50.770
And Campbell has had nothing but positive
things to say about the film, telling Collider,

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.240
"[Evil Dead Rise] does not suck in the least.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.789
Lee Cronin did a great job.

00:04:54.789 --> 00:04:56.949
... It's a very European 'Evil Dead.'"

00:04:56.949 --> 00:05:00.919
We're assuming Campbell is referencing European
horror sensibilities, although we don't know

00:05:00.919 --> 00:05:05.320
if he's talking about Italian giallo, French
Extremity, or some other style.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.789
Whatever we're getting, it's sure to be scary.

00:05:07.789 --> 00:05:08.789
Raimi told /Film,

00:05:08.789 --> 00:05:12.017
"It's terrifying, and it's going to knock
people's socks off."

00:05:12.336 --> 00:05:17.393
If you know anything about the Evil Dead series,
then you know it's not exactly a PG-rated franchise.

00:05:17.393 --> 00:05:22.600
The first film scared up the dreaded NC-17,
with the subsequent entries all earning an

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.020
R-rating with their severed limbs and geysers
of gore.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.220
So what will Evil Dead Rise be rated?

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:32.620
Will it compare to previous entries, or will
it go the route of so many modern movies and

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.220
play it safe with an audience-friendly PG-13?

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.830
Well, never fear, Deadite diehards.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.890
Evil Dead Rise is gonna keep things nasty.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:45.370
According to Fangoria, the 2023 film is officially
rated R. How come?

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:50.080
As you might expect, Lee Cronin's upcoming
movie earned the big bad R due to "strong

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.600
bloody horror violence and gore, and some
language."

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:56.120
Obviously, you can't have an Evil Dead film
without delivering on the kills.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:00.950
Well, Army of Darkness isn't exactly the hardest
R, but from everything we've heard, it seems

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:06.373
likely this one will have more in common with
the first two films and Fede Álvarez's installment.

00:06:06.373 --> 00:06:08.289
If you're at work, watch out.

00:06:08.289 --> 00:06:11.229
The red band trailer for Evil Dead Rise isn't
messing around.

00:06:11.229 --> 00:06:15.110
The trailer begins with possessed mother Ellie,
cooking the world's worst batch of scrambled

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:19.080
eggs and describing a lovely dream ... where
she violently murders her whole family.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:23.389
Clearly, paging through the Necronomicon and
playing that old creepy record her kid found

00:06:23.389 --> 00:06:24.650
was a mistake.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.400
It's always a mistake.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.190
From there, we watch as scalps get ripped
from heads, Deadites swallow shards of glass,

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:36.074
and our bloodied hero Beth guarding a group
of poor kids from their very undead mom.

00:06:36.074 --> 00:06:37.074
"Mom?"

00:06:37.192 --> 00:06:39.341
"Mommy's with the maggots now."

00:06:39.419 --> 00:06:43.880
Yes, that Evil Dead staple — the chainsaw
— does make an appearance, promising plenty

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:48.330
of severed limbs and arterial sprays, and
we're also terrified to see what happens with

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:49.800
that cheese grater.

00:06:50.095 --> 00:06:54.200
When it comes to iconic horror franchises,
few are as extensive as the Evil Dead.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:59.710
This series has 5 movies of varying continuity,
a three-season television series, and multiple

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:00.720
video games.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:05.467
"You're kind of like a young me.

00:07:05.604 --> 00:07:07.204
Deadites ruined your life and you're hot as
hell."

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:11.470
Thanks to all this content, the Evil Dead
storyline can be a bit confusing for new fans

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:15.590
to wrap their head around.The very first Evil
Dead movie pits Ash Williams and his friends

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:19.479
against otherworldly demons while they're
stuck in a remote woodland cabin.

00:07:19.479 --> 00:07:24.479
With Ash as the only survivor, his story continues
into the events of Evil Dead II and Army of

00:07:24.479 --> 00:07:29.294
Darkness as he slowly and surely becomes a
Deadite-killing, chainsaw-handed hero.

00:07:29.294 --> 00:07:33.464
"Now, let's talk about how I get back home."

00:07:33.464 --> 00:07:37.710
Following his time in the Middle Ages during
Army of Darkness, Ash spends the next 30 years

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:42.570
as a total loser working at ValueStop before
accidentally reading from the Necronomicon

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:46.020
once again to initiate the plot of Ash vs
Evil Dead.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.030
Now, it's important to understand that the
world of Evil Dead Rise is supposedly linked

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:54.720
to the original trilogy rather than the 2013
reboot titled Evil Dead.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.000
Some key elements are carried over from what
came before, however, such as the Necronomicon

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.443
and the appearance of horrifying Deadites.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:06.419
Evil Dead Rise has had a slightly complicated
development history, as have many installments

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:09.449
in this franchise since its beginnings in
1981.

00:08:09.449 --> 00:08:14.360
This whole mess started back in 2013 after
director Fede Álvarez was given free rein

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.259
to make his own remake of the original film.

00:08:17.259 --> 00:08:21.510
Evil Dead reimagines the events of the first
movie with an emphasis on realistic gore,

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.479
nuanced characters, and more modern horror.

00:08:24.479 --> 00:08:28.740
Additionally, completely new characters are
added to the canon including new heroine Mia

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.801
Allen, although Ash Williams himself does
make a small cameo appearance in a post-credits scene.

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:37.730
Following the release of Evil Dead, Álvarez
was slated to make a sequel to his reboot

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:42.080
with the backing of Sam Raimi and Bruce Campbell,
but things stalled as Álvarez found success

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.209
with his own original Don't Breathe series.

00:08:44.209 --> 00:08:49.200
The Uruguayan filmmaker even tweeted a poll
back in 2018 asking fans which of his big

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.585
movies they'd want to see a sequel of and
then expressed his disappointment in the results.

00:08:53.585 --> 00:08:54.725
He told MovieWeb,

00:08:54.725 --> 00:08:57.899
"When I tweeted that I was interested in seeing
what people prefer.

00:08:57.899 --> 00:09:00.160
[...] Unfortunately, 'Evil Dead 2' won.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.626
Which, I guess I would have preferred 'Don't
Breathe 2' to win because it's one of my own creations.

00:09:04.626 --> 00:09:06.930
Obviously 'Evil Dead' has the bigger following.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:08.040
So that's what happened."

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:12.430
It seems he ultimately decided to go his own
way, since that proposed sequel morphed into

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:17.652
an entirely new spin-off movie now known as
Evil Dead Rise without Álvarez at the helm.

00:09:17.998 --> 00:09:22.040
There's something special about bloody, gory
cult horror movies that get certain types

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.790
of people frothing at the mouth.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:27.980
Evil Dead has proven to be one of the most
popular franchises of its kind with seemingly

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:32.600
endless fans inspired by the way Sam Raimi
and Bruce Campbell merged the genres of horror

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.649
and comedy seamlessly together.

00:09:34.649 --> 00:09:38.700
Indie filmmakers everywhere have cited Evil
Dead as a fundamental touchstone of their

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:43.120
own desire to make no-budget movies, with
some pretty big names in entertainment pointing

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:48.030
to Raimi's work as inspiration such as Peter
Jackson and Edgar Wright.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:52.070
Even filmmakers as prestigious as the Coen
brothers got their start editing for Sam Raimi

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.730
on The Evil Dead — at least, Joel did, according
to the story.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:10:00.010
The filmmaking style of The Evil Dead even
left an impact on the Coens' own work, most

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:03.450
notably in their films Blood Simple and Raising
Arizona.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:08.290
That said, this is a franchise that has consistently
produced commercially successful and critically

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.440
acclaimed content that fans can't get enough
of.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:16.519
Overall, the franchise has made over $150
million on a relatively small budget.

00:10:16.519 --> 00:10:20.890
Furthermore, the films are constantly screened
at fan events and around Halloween, which

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:24.910
shows just how much people love to see Deadites
get cut in half with a chainsaw.

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:27.284
The newest installment will no doubt be just
as…

00:10:27.284 --> 00:10:28.332
"Groovy."

